# Project Coding Rules

## Code Comments
- All code comments, docstrings, and inline documentation MUST be written in English
- This applies to:
  - Function and class docstrings
  - Inline comments
  - TODO comments
  - Code explanations
  - Variable descriptions

## Language Preference
- Code: English
- Comments: English
- Documentation: English
- Variable names: English
- Function names: English

## Exception
- User-facing strings (UI messages, error messages shown to users) can be in any language as needed for the application

## Code Modification Workflow
- When user asks questions or describes problems, DO NOT immediately make code changes
- First: Analyze the problem, understand the context, ask clarifying questions if needed
- Second: Propose solutions or explain the approach
- Third: Wait for explicit user command (like "do it", "fix it", "implement") before making any code changes
- Only make code changes when user explicitly requests them
- If user asks "is this correct?" or "should I do this?" - provide analysis and recommendations, but do NOT implement changes

## Code Style & Formatting
- Follow PEP 8 style guide for Python code
- Use 4 spaces for indentation (no tabs)
- Maximum line length: 120 characters (prefer 100 when possible)
- Use double quotes for strings (consistent with Django conventions)
